{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3f4af1bb55fb0e07df543d85bc12db5227e537ef3aa6ec865720210834dcb08d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Teams write session-scoped files under .kkirikkiri/teams/{team_name}/ (TEAM_PLAN.md, TEAM_PROGRESS.md, TEAM_FINDINGS.md, report.md), while saved teams persist cross-session under .kkirikkiri/shared/saved-teams/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44b3ffddb82b45d500b26d1a11689fd4d67a34338ed0d2089e69bdfea443be95"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The validation loop runs at most two rounds by default: round 1 is the original team, round 2 an auto-judge choosing keep, full replacement, or partial swap; further rounds need explicit approval."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4eb4f4f0e76508af22b9aaa7e34e3254c8c9eb3aae69a2f908f27aa336195e19"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Multi-model support appears to work by shelling out to installed external CLIs (Codex, agy, grok, gjc) with per-provider flags and model-override env vars like KKIRIKKIRI_GROK_MODEL."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5eda18cb33add8db489a45a606ee3f61c21e647f33145cfd45b4449e0678fe65"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is invoked via a /kkirikkiri slash command (e.g. '/kkirikkiri build me a research team') after installing from a plugin marketplace."},{"claim_ids":["clm_69210465d4e48c55c184d3b0ee9154dca80b249543ef129e81d26fe77bdbce7e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The opt-in preparation pilot generates cards and Agent requests from one approved plan but is explicitly not a runtime permission sandbox, and no OS sandbox or write serialization for concurrent sessions is newly guaranteed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8584bbe79eddc0ddec2ae35ed860cfa49f3d136d8cd9e6bedbd54cb2d0bed7bd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Execution follows an eight-step pipeline: intent/preset matching, parallel environment scan, interview, team composition, user confirmation, shared-memory init, quality validation, and report collection."},{"claim_ids":["clm_95a653ba569c170b4303dfea9742f8f672457d1cd8fe96567894ebf7a9ad2632"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"kkirikkiri is a Claude Code plugin that takes a plain-language goal, asks only for missing decisions, scans the environment, and runs an approved agent team or Workflow."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a6af3e7ea044000ddd3793fdb33078ae900a109006e3725494cf3f174b4383b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Two execution substrates are offered: a live collaborating Agent Teams mode or a deterministic Workflow pipeline for high-volume fan-out work; the user picks between them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a5186fdfe2d8d001b2c69f34b2d7fa52e1100420ca65e28d92d5c9fcc0bcf6be"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Requires Claude Code with the CLAUDE_CODE_EXPERIMENTAL_AGENT_TEAMS=1 env flag and Node.js; tmux is optional, and external CLIs (Codex, Antigravity agy, Grok) are optional since Claude alone can run the full team."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ed8461dbe64fcabfaa6586e88ce08e6a69d0f87226846da8050a5f0d430ad37e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Five built-in presets (Research, Development, Analysis, Content, Product/PM) are matched by natural-language trigger words and serve only as starting points for the final team."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3f4af1bb55fb0e07df543d85bc12db5227e537ef3aa6ec865720210834dcb08d","clm_44b3ffddb82b45d500b26d1a11689fd4d67a34338ed0d2089e69bdfea443be95","clm_4eb4f4f0e76508af22b9aaa7e34e3254c8c9eb3aae69a2f908f27aa336195e19","clm_5eda18cb33add8db489a45a606ee3f61c21e647f33145cfd45b4449e0678fe65","clm_69210465d4e48c55c184d3b0ee9154dca80b249543ef129e81d26fe77bdbce7e","clm_8584bbe79eddc0ddec2ae35ed860cfa49f3d136d8cd9e6bedbd54cb2d0bed7bd","clm_95a653ba569c170b4303dfea9742f8f672457d1cd8fe96567894ebf7a9ad2632","clm_9a6af3e7ea044000ddd3793fdb33078ae900a109006e3725494cf3f174b4383b","clm_a5186fdfe2d8d001b2c69f34b2d7fa52e1100420ca65e28d92d5c9fcc0bcf6be","clm_ed8461dbe64fcabfaa6586e88ce08e6a69d0f87226846da8050a5f0d430ad37e"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:49:09Z","created_by_operation":"op_e917682f1a204ae39e15c6542eb282a5","id":"pg_2bb54ca9d8d1518d998bbd6c5